# vibecode fresh-clone marker — read by .claude/hooks/session-start.sh (step 0).
#
# The one-time "fresh clone" bootstrap (reset framework-history docs from
# templates, git init, baseline manifest, initial commit) runs ONLY when ALL
# of these hold:
#   1. PROJECT_ROOT has no .git (neither dir nor file) and is not inside
#      any git work tree
#   2. .vibecode/VERSION does not exist (no /vibe-update baseline yet)
#   3. this marker exists AND every path listed below exists
#
# Why this is safe: the listed paths are vibecode's OWN meta-plans. They exist
# only in a full clone of the vibecode source repo (clone → rm -rf .git), never
# in a project the framework was layered into by copying .claude/ + .vibecode/.
# The bootstrap deletes docs/architecture/*-plan.md, so after the first run
# condition 3 is false and the branch can never fire again.
#
# Maintainers: if you rename/archive one of these plans, update this list —
# otherwise the bootstrap silently stops running (fail-safe, never fail-open).
# One relative path per line; '#' lines and blank lines are ignored.
docs/architecture/clone-workflow-plan.md
docs/architecture/multi-ai-plan-consultation-plan.md
